From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 13:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: a733: cubie-a7s: reserve a ramoops window

A board that the watchdog resets, or that panics and reboots after 10 s,
comes back with no trace of why: the kernel log was in RAM, and nobody
was at the serial console. pstore keeps the panic, the oops and the
console of the previous boot in a reserved DRAM window that survives the
warm reset; the kernel side is PSTORE, PSTORE_CONSOLE and PSTORE_RAM in
the kernel config (kernel/6.18/config). This patch gives ramoops its window.

WHERE EACH VALUE COMES FROM

  * The binding: Documentation/devicetree/bindings/reserved-memory/ramoops.yaml:
    a reserved-memory child with compatible "ramoops".
  * 0x60000000: inside the first GiB of DRAM (memory starts at
    0x40000000), so it exists on every memory population; above U-Boot's
    bootm_size window (SDRAM 0x40000000 + BOOTM_SIZE 0xa000000,
    include/configs/sunxi-common.h in the boot chain), so booti does not
    place the kernel, fdt or initrd there; and on the 8 GiB board on 2026-09-14 a
    1 MiB pattern there was kept whole across a U-Boot `reset` (a WDT0
    reset) and a WDT0 timeout, while 0x80000000 and 0x180000000 changed in
    part.
  * console-size 0x40000 and ecc-size 16: the most frequent values among
    the ramoops nodes in arch/arm64/boot/dts (console-size 0x40000 in 19
    nodes, ecc-size 16 in 18). ECC because other DRAM regions were
    rewritten in part across a reset.
  * record-size 0x20000 (10 upstream nodes; 0x1000 is more frequent, 13):
    with PSTORE_COMPRESS, pstore_dump() fills a part with up to 100/60 of
    the record's data area (bufsize: the record minus its header and ECC,
    fs/pstore/platform.c and ram.c) of log before compressing, so a 128 KiB
    record keeps a whole panic in one part.

No A523 value: no sun55i DT carries a ramoops node. Not taken from the
vendor BSP.

WHAT THIS DOES NOT COVER

  * A power cycle loses the window.
  * A hang that stops the console before WDT0 fires leaves the console
    record where the log stopped.

VERIFIED HERE: applies with fuzz 0 on top of the full series; the board
dts, preprocessed with cpp and built with dtc, reads back
/reserved-memory/ramoops@60000000 with reg <0 0x60000000 0 0x100000> and
compatible "ramoops".

VERIFIED ON HARDWARE (2026-09-14, the 8 GiB board, test build of this series): after
`systemctl reboot` -- by the source (TF-A plat/allwinner/common/
sunxi_native_pm.c) BL31's PSCI SYSTEM_RESET, not the
WDT0 resets the window was first measured across -- console-ramoops held the
boot's last lines; after a sysrq panic dmesg-ramoops held Panic#1 with the
panic line, in one part; after PID 1 froze and WDT0 reset the board,
console-ramoops ended with `watchdog did not stop!`.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
@@ -625,6 +625,25 @@
 		scp@48100000 {
 			reg = <0x0 0x48100000 0x0 0x00100000>;
 		};
+
+		/*
+		 * pstore: the panic, oops and console log of the previous boot.
+		 * 0x60000000 is inside the first GiB, so every memory population
+		 * has it; above U-Boot's bootm_size window (0x40000000 + 0xa000000,
+		 * include/configs/sunxi-common.h), so booti does not load there; and
+		 * it was kept whole across a WDT0 reset and a WDT0 timeout on the
+		 * 8 GiB board, where
+		 * other DRAM regions changed in part. console-size and ecc-size are
+		 * the values most upstream arm64 ramoops nodes use; a 128 KiB record
+		 * holds a whole panic dump in one compressed part (fs/pstore/platform.c).
+		 */
+		ramoops@60000000 {
+			compatible = "ramoops";
+			reg = <0x0 0x60000000 0x0 0x00100000>;
+			record-size = <0x20000>;
+			console-size = <0x40000>;
+			ecc-size = <16>;
+		};
 	};
 
 	/*
